.TH AGNSH 1 "August 2026" "agnoshi 1.9.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agnsh \- AI-native natural language shell for AGNOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agnsh
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ -c
.IR COMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agnsh
translates natural language into system commands with human oversight,
security approval workflows, and full audit logging.
.PP
Without arguments, starts an interactive shell. The prompt carries the
current mode (e.g.
.BR [ASSIST]\ > ).
Type natural language to see the proposed shell command, its risk level
.RB ( [LOW] " / " [MED] " / " [HIGH] " / " [CRIT] ),
and a
.B Hint:
line when the translation isn't directly runnable (LLM-routed question,
unsupported pipeline, or translator safety rejection).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -c, --command \fICMD\fR
Execute one command and exit.
.TP
.B -v, --version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.B --mode \fINAME\fR
Run under mode \fINAME\fR (auto, assist, human, strict). An unrecognised
name is an error and agnsh exits non-zero \(em it is never silently
downgraded to a more permissive mode.
.SH MODES
Every mode parses, classifies, reports risk and writes an audit record.
What the mode changes is whether a program launch is confirmed first.
.TP
.B human
Confirms every program launch with a y/n prompt. It does not hand you a
raw shell and does not disable classification.
.TP
.B assist
Default. Parses and reports the proposed command and its risk. Program
launches proceed without a confirmation prompt.
.TP
.B auto
As assist, without the assist framing. Program launches proceed without a
confirmation prompt.
.TP
.B strict
Most conservative: every program launch requires a y/n confirmation.
.PP
.B NOTE:
a high-risk natural-language translation reports
.I "Approval required"
but is never executed \(em the natural-language path does not execute at
all yet, so no approval prompt appears for it in any mode.
.SH BUILTINS
.TP
.B help
Show built-in commands.
.TP
.B clear
Clear screen.
.TP
.B exit, quit
Exit shell.
.TP
.B history
Show command history.
.TP
.B mode [NAME]
Show or change operating mode (human, assist, auto, strict).
.TP
.B run \fIPATH\fR
Run a program from an absolute path. The only execution path on a Linux
host; on AGNOS, bareword \fB/bin/\fIname\fR, two-stage pipelines
.RB ( "cmd1 | cmd2" ),
output redirection
.RB ( "cmd > file" )
and background jobs
.RB ( "prog &" )
also execute.
.TP
.B reboot, poweroff, halt
Platform power control (AGNOS).
.SH PERMISSIONS
Every command is classified into one of six levels:
.TP
.B SAFE
No state change (cd, echo, help).
.TP
.B READ_ONLY
System queries (ls, cat, ps).
.TP
.B USER_WRITE
Modifies user files (cp, mv, touch).
.TP
.B SYSTEM_WRITE
Modifies system paths (requires approval).
.TP
.B ADMIN
Requires sudo (requires approval).
.TP
.B BLOCKED
Never allowed for AI (rm -rf, dd, mkfs, chmod, chown).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.agnsh_history
Command history (mode 0600).
.TP
.I ~/.agnsh_audit.log
Structured JSON audit log, mode 0600, opened O_NOFOLLOW. Each line carries
timestamp, user, mode, input, action, approved (0/1), result, and
exit_code (JSON null when the record describes something that never ran).
.I result
comes from one of two disjoint sets \(em parse-time (proposed,
needs_approval, blocked, needs_llm, needs_exec, rejected_safety) or
exec-time (launched, executed, failed, error, denied).
.PP
When
.B $HOME
is unset, this and the history file fall back to
.IR /tmp/agnsh_audit.log. "" uid
and
.IR /tmp/agnsh_history. "" uid
\(em degraded operation, not a supported configuration.
.SH AUTHOR
Written for the AGNOS project.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR sudo (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
